  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Wood Charm Gu’s advancement recipes fuse hundred-year and thousand-year lifespan Gu into higher Wood Charm ranks, but Gu Masters who find lifespan Gu usually use it on themselves instead. A hundred years lifespan Gu adds a hundred years of life, and a thousand years lifespan Gu adds a thousand. Lifespan Gu are extremely rare and sought after. They represent long life without granting undying existence.",
        "chapters": [
          126
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_wood_charm_gu",
          "fac_gu_masters"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Under ordinary conditions a human lifespan is about a hundred years, and lifespan Gu is the preferred extension method, though they remain hard to find.",
        "chapters": [
          367
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Lifespan Gu are hard to find, their locations are fixed, and only heaven and earth create them in limited supply. After surveying other extension methods, Spectral Soul’s critique still treats lifespan Gu as the best choice. Venerables exhaust natural stocks and then invent substitutes.",
        "chapters": [
          599
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "natural-production",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "They are only mortal Gu. Their production conditions vary widely, Gu Immortals often find them only by luck, and mortal Gu Masters often obtain them first.",
        "chapters": [
          778
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "natural-production",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_mortal_gu",
          "sys_gu_immortal"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Musing over Giant Sun’s true inheritance, Spectral Soul Demon Venerable reflects that heaven’s will is vicious and governs lifespan Gu’s output, so fewer and fewer are being produced.",
        "chapters": [
          1015
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "natural-production",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_spectral_soul_demon_venerable"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Lifespan Gu is a heaven path Gu worm that people cannot refine. Even in a venerable’s era, natural production of lifespan Gu falls while the venerable lives.",
        "chapters": [
          2085
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "heaven-path",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_worms"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A Gu cultivator’s lifespan is in fact heaven path dao marks.",
        "chapters": [
          2275
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "heaven-path",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
